scenes.gallery.components.narrative.text:
The sound of the lobby fades as you step into the gallery. Brass lamps illuminate a row of empty display stands.

{{case}}

The doorway back to the lobby is to the west.

{{inspection}}

scenes.old-harbour.narrative:
A small rowing boat knocks against the quay. Beyond the harbour mouth, pale bars of sand shift beneath the waves. A red buoy bobs between them.

The harbour chart shows which side of the shallows to take. Carry it with you and inspect it before rowing out.

{{inspection}}

scenes.shoals.narrative:
The oars scrape over sand on either side of the channel. You ease past the red buoy, where the current tugs the boat sideways.

The chart marks the turn here. North of the buoy, a split rock stands at the bend that leads to the landing.

{{inspection}}

scenes.north-cliff-landing.narrative:
The boat slips past the split rock and into still water below the north cliffs. You pull it onto a strip of shingle and tie the painter to an iron ring set into the stone.

Looking back, you can trace the narrow channel all the way to the red buoy. From shore, it would have been easy to miss.

{{inspection}}
